  "prefLabel": "Plc 1806.05 Certified Property Assessor Assistant Duties",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Plc 1806.05 Certified Property Assessor Assistant Duties.\n\n(a) For revaluation or assessing services, under the guidance and oversight of a certified property assessor or certified property assessor supervisor, a certified property assessor assistant may assist with:\n\n(1) Assessing services as defined in Plc 1802.08;\n\n(2) Sale validation; and\n\n(3) The training of a building measurer and lister.\n\n(b) A certified property assessor assistant shall not:\n\n(1) Adjust an assessment except under the supervision of a certified property assessor or certified property assessor supervisor;\n\n(2) Oversee a final field review as defined in Plc 1802.19;\n\n(3) Oversee a revaluation informal review process or conduct abatement reviews; or\n\n(4) Represent a municipality in the defense of assessed values, provided that a certified property assessor assistant may assist a certified property assessor or certified property assessor supervisor in such defense.\n\nSource. #14330, eff 9-22-25, EXPIRES: 9-22-35",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/plc1800.html"
